# SGLang Integration for Denial of Wallet

## Purpose

This document defines how SGLang can be integrated into **Denial of Wallet — Economic Security for Autonomous AI Agents**.

The goal is not to make SGLang a dependency of the core security platform. Instead, SGLang is an **optional real inference/serving layer** that gives Denial of Wallet a realistic environment in which to observe, predict, and control AI-agent spending.

> **Core idea:** Denial of Wallet protects the economic boundary between an autonomous agent and its model-serving infrastructure.

---

# 1. What is SGLang?

SGLang is a high-performance serving framework for large language and multimodal models. It provides model serving, high-throughput inference, batching, parallelism, and an OpenAI-compatible API.

The current SGLang quickstart documents an OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions` endpoint and examples using the OpenAI Python client.

Official references:

- SGLang repository: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang
- SGLang quickstart: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/docs/docs/get-started/quickstart.mdx
- SGLang Model Gateway: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/docs/advanced_features/sgl_model_gateway.md

