# 2. Why SGLang Fits Denial of Wallet

Denial of Wallet needs to observe real AI inference behavior.

Our system needs signals such as:

- request frequency
- input tokens
- output tokens
- model used
- latency
- tool activity
- request concurrency
- token throughput
- estimated economic cost

A real inference server gives us a much stronger demonstration than manually inserting fake database events.

Instead of:

```text
Fake Event Generator
        ↓
usage_events
```

we can eventually have:

```text
AI Agent
    ↓
Denial of Wallet Gateway
    ↓
SGLang
    ↓
Real Model Inference
    ↓
Telemetry
    ↓
Cost / Risk / Policy
```

This allows the hackathon demo to show that the platform can protect a real model-serving workflow.

