# 6. Main SGLang Use Cases in Denial of Wallet

## Use Case 1 — Real Telemetry Source

SGLang becomes the source of actual inference traffic.

Denial of Wallet records:

```text
request timestamp
model
input tokens
output tokens
latency
request rate
concurrency
```

These become `usage_events`.

## Use Case 2 — Real Cost Measurement

Instead of trusting:

```json
{
  "estimated_cost": 0.08
}
```

from an agent, Denial of Wallet can calculate cost from:

```text
model
+
input tokens
+
output tokens
+
pricing configuration
```

This is much safer.

Conceptually:

```text
SGLang request
      |
      v
Token usage
      |
      v
Pricing Engine
      |
      v
Trusted economic cost
```

This is especially important because an attacker should not be able to simply report:

```text
estimated_cost = 0
```

to hide its actual consumption.

## Use Case 3 — Attack Simulation

Our attack simulator can eventually generate real requests against the SGLang server.

Example:

```text
Normal mode

5 requests/min
       ↓
SGLang
       ↓
Telemetry
       ↓
LOW RISK
```

Then:

```text
Attack mode

200 requests/min
       ↓
SGLang
       ↓
Telemetry spike
       ↓
Cost acceleration
       ↓
HIGH/CRITICAL RISK
```

This creates a real end-to-end attack demonstration.

## Use Case 4 — Policy Enforcement

Denial of Wallet can make decisions before forwarding requests to SGLang.

For example:

```text
Incoming request
       |
       v
Risk = 25
       |
       v
ALLOW
       |
       v
SGLang
```

During an attack:

```text
Incoming request
       |
       v
Risk = 72
       |
       v
THROTTLE
       |
       v
SGLang
```

At extreme risk:

```text
Incoming request
       |
       v
Risk = 97
       |
       v
BLOCK
```

The security decision is made by Denial of Wallet, not by the model.

## Use Case 5 — Model Downgrade

Suppose:

```text
Current model:
expensive-model

Risk:
88

Projected burn:
$120/hour
```

The Policy Engine could recommend:

```text
MODEL_DOWNGRADE
```

The gateway can route subsequent requests to a cheaper model.

Conceptually:

```text
                    POLICY ENGINE
                          |
                  MODEL_DOWNGRADE
                          |
             +------------+------------+
             |                         |
             v                         v
      expensive model           cheaper model
             |                         |
             +------------+------------+
                          |
                          v
                       SGLang
```

This allows Denial of Wallet to reduce economic exposure while keeping the agent operational.

## Use Case 6 — Digital Twin Validation

The Digital Twin can simulate:

```text
Current behavior
Attack continues
Throttle
Block
Model downgrade
```

For example:

```text
                DIGITAL TWIN
                     |
        +------------+------------+
        |            |            |
        v            v            v
      Normal      Attack       Throttle
        |            |            |
        v            v            v
      $10/h        $180/h        $18/h
        |            |            |
        v            v            v
     LOW RISK     CRITICAL      MEDIUM
```

The Digital Twin can then say:

> If we do nothing, the agent is projected to exhaust its $100 budget in 34 minutes. Throttling reduces projected cost by 84%.

This turns the Digital Twin into a **decision-support system**, rather than a visualization.

