# 7. SGLang Model Gateway

SGLang also provides a Model Gateway with routing and middleware capabilities.

Its current documentation describes OpenAI-compatible routing, multi-model inference gateway functionality, and WASM middleware for request/response processing. The middleware use cases include authentication, rate limiting, request modification, logging, and rejecting requests.

This creates a possible future architecture:

```text
Agent
  ↓
SGLang Model Gateway
  ↓
Denial of Wallet controls
  ↓
SGLang workers
  ↓
Models
```

However:

## We should NOT start here.

For the hackathon MVP, keep the architecture simple:

```text
Agent
  ↓
Denial of Wallet
  ↓
SGLang
  ↓
Model
```

This makes our security boundary easier to explain and demonstrate.

---

# 8. Proposed Integration Layer

Add this only when the core pipeline is stable:

```text
backend/
└── app/
    └── integrations/
        └── sglang.py
```

The adapter should handle only:

```text
connect to SGLang
send inference request
receive response
extract usage/latency information
normalize telemetry
```

It should NOT contain:

```text
risk calculations
attack detection
policy decisions
Digital Twin logic
```

Those belong to the existing services.

Target flow:

```text
SGLang Adapter
      |
      v
Normalized Telemetry
      |
      v
Telemetry Service
      |
      v
Cost Engine
      |
      v
Attack Detector
      |
      v
Risk Engine
      |
      v
Digital Twin / Policy
```

This keeps SGLang replaceable.

---

# 9. Why SGLang Should Remain Optional

Denial of Wallet should work with multiple inference providers.

Potential future sources:

```text
SGLang
OpenAI
Anthropic
vLLM
Ollama
other OpenAI-compatible servers
```

Therefore:

```text
                Denial of Wallet
                       |
             Inference Adapter
                       |
       +---------------+---------------+
       |               |               |
       v               v               v
    SGLang           OpenAI          vLLM
```

The economic security layer stays the same.

Only the adapter changes.

> **Denial of Wallet is not an SGLang security product. It is an economic security layer for autonomous AI agents.**

SGLang is our strongest real-inference demonstration.

